────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
WEB SOURCE (the specification)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  web/src/components/ui/PinButton.tsx — a tiny, focusable icon-only (or icon+label) toggle that pins /
  unpins a single row through the unified pin store. Data:
    • usePinned(itemType, context)  → /pinned?type=…[&context=…] → PinnedItem[] (defaulted to [])
      isPinned = pinned.some(p => String(p.item_id) === String(itemId))
    • useTogglePin(itemType)         → POST /pinned (pin) / DELETE /pinned/{id} (unpin); toggle.isPending
    • useTranslation                 → t('pin.pin'|'pin.unpin'|'pin.pinned')
  Render: <Tooltip content=tooltipLabel><button aria-pressed=isPinned aria-label=tooltipLabel
    disabled=toggle.isPending> <Icon = isPinned ? PinOff : Pin> {showLabel && <span>Pin|Pinned</span>}.
  Props: itemType, itemId, context?, size?('sm'|'md'), showLabel?, className?. Click stops propagation
  (the row is often a navigation target) and bails while toggle.isPending.

