PARITY DISPOSITION (Honesty Covenant #5 — No parity shortcuts cuts both ways)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  The web <PinButton> is a data-bound toggle that destructures only `data: pinned = []`, so it SWALLOWS
  the usePinned query's loading / error into the unpinned default and NEVER renders a skeleton, a
  QueryError panel, or an empty placeholder — the button is ALWAYS shown. The native surface keeps that
  exact contract (the button is never hidden; isPinned reads the best-available — cached during a refresh
  — set; unknown ⇒ not pinned) AND, per the P4 leaf states contract, surfaces the freshness the web
  swallows as a small, gated corner badge (offline → error → stale precedence) layered OVER the
  unconditionally-rendered button — exactly as the in-tree sibling data-bound surface CookieConsentBanner
  (0115) layers its freshness chip over the cached value. Reproduced REAL branches: unpinned, pinned,
  busy (web toggle.isPending → disabled+dimmed), cold-load (button-sized spinner, never a blank box;
  resolves to unpinned when the set is empty, web `pinned = []`), and the cached stale/offline/error
  freshness axis with a VoiceOver Retry action + one-shot stale auto-refresh. Charts/maps: none in source
  → none here.

